From 5856e3d289171b0d235e3b572679b70ffc3600d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahmed Al-Nassif <mr.ahmed.nassif@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 23:02:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/24] f2fs: Enlarge min_fsync_blocks to 20

In OPPO's kernel:
enlarge min_fsync_blocks to optimize performance
  - yanwu@TECH.Storage.FS.oF2FS, 2019/08/12

Huawei is also doing this in their production kernel.

If this optimization is good for them and shipped
with their devices, it should be good for us.

Signed-off-by: Jesse Chan <jc@linux.com>
Signed-off-by: Adithya R <gh0strider.2k18.reborn@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Ahmed Al-Nassif <mr.ahmed.nassif@gmail.com>
---
 fs/f2fs/segment.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/f2fs/segment.h b/fs/f2fs/segment.h
index 904625112..2a3a858d0 100644
--- a/fs/f2fs/segment.h
+++ b/fs/f2fs/segment.h
@@ -710,7 +710,7 @@ static inline int utilization(struct f2fs_sb_info *sbi)
  * F2FS_IPU_DISABLE - disable IPU. (=default option in LFS mode)
  */
 #define DEF_MIN_IPU_UTIL	70
-#define DEF_MIN_FSYNC_BLOCKS	8
+#define DEF_MIN_FSYNC_BLOCKS	20
 #define DEF_MIN_HOT_BLOCKS	16
 
 #define SMALL_VOLUME_SEGMENTS	(16 * 512)	/* 16GB */
-- 
2.55.0

